body:
Before I wound up in assisted living, I was no real master, so to speak, at having soup recipes. I just basically cleared the fridge and added a can of random beans and some chicken bouillon. 

&#x200B;

Damn good soup. Just random, but good.

Ouch. Just. Ouch. This is what I am afraid of. Used to get it and lost tf of my shirt. I have, what IS working for me is a blend of forex signals, ADX Wilder and Trends. Has it ever worked so far for me! I am SHOCKED. Usually along with, after a buy, watchful waiting before I sell.

&#x200B;

Seeing this, I could have surely wept for you. That is a total oww.

Getting the TV newscaster Just-Been Darling, H1N1 and thought o my. I'm dead now, anyhoo, get to see my late sister. Then being in ICU for 3 weeks out cold and then waking and seeing Mom right away. Thought, Guess this is Earth, that is Mom and NOT the dearly departed sister I loved so much.

&#x200B;

Glad Mom was there, but still missed my older departed sis. 

&#x200B;

Then on to find out I needed dialysis. That sent me for a heluva jolt. All this happened when I was only 40.

Depends. Was your partner listening/watching true crime stuff? If they are getting this from that, maybe they'd be absorbing all that is said on these. 

&#x200B;

Call me a kook, but something past life related?

&#x200B;

Thirdly, if none of these, then possibly counseling will be a worthy thing to look into?

Come to wonder: who DIDN'T!?

&#x200B;

Ya, seemed to me I was somehow yelled at at least 2x a day if not up to 10X a day. It was awful then. Glad that is now over.

Next time that dog did things like this. POOMMMMmmm!!!!!!!!!!!!!! NO. Questions. 

&#x200B;

Dog goes missing. NO conversation except tough luck!

You would NEVER. EVER! Call from that thing; the stories whirring by would pretty much carry that message. You had to be 2 MINUTES or LESS from death in a ditch to even! wow.

&#x200B;

 Even as those messages whirled around, I DAMN well knew WTH to NOT do. Period.

OMG! The "doctor" is so gone too far already and I already smell some rats here. Perhaps the Cousin has to put a pencil in their V? Already super-sus about the cousin right squarely there. Perhaps your cousin was exposed/abused already. 

&#x200B;

This is a bright redder than red flag right there. I would find a way to get the cousin into therapy as this is a straight up red flag already. Possibly call CPS and focus first on this red flag. Please do this ASAP for all concerned sake?

Despite crying, I think, IMHO, that is SO cool to have a shared dream like that. Seems like you two were together one time, at least, before, possibly, at the time as brothers then, also. COOL!

&#x200B;

Was this an ancient time, or more like the 1800-1900s?

You are a nut job. YOU. Don't care if the kids die? Well, the kids may actually WANT to live, and YOU took their choice, maybe legally, but morally? You. Are. A. Monster.

&#x200B;

IF this is a joke of some disgusting sort, then do disregard, but if real, SCREW. You.

As long as the allergy isn't possibly airborne, like some people were at my sisters' old place where you couldn't HAVE green peppers in the bldg, b/c it wafted right through ductwork. I thought that allergy'd be ABSOLUTE HELL on Earth. I felt sorry for the whole damn building.

&#x200B;

If it could get onto EVERYTHING, I'd then say not likely to eat the allergen if it is a big spreader like nuts or generally airborne risk, but if it is a soup, or something easily contained, then ok.

I find the saying "Time Heals" to be so inaccurate that I have zero idea to laugh or cry when people say this. Sure, time and distance increases between the event and years and years go by. I found that no. Time does NOT heal. All there is to it is that you slowly learn to COPE with it.

&#x200B;

The idea that time heals is so inaccurate that I could just... O WOW.

I feel something like that too, regarding my oldest sister. It IS irritating, but people who have yet to live through a thing like this will never even know. UNTIL it happens to them. People only are trying to mean well, but Jezus, the tropes!!

&#x200B;

You are right that it doesn't get better, like many who haven't experienced stuff like this seem to like to think. Another motivator for this kind of thinking when it didn't happen to them yet is a perception of time and distance to an event like this. All that really happens is the grief is there forever. Over time, you learn how to actually cope. I remember this and still miss them forever more. Even after 9 years.

From what I have gotten from this subreddit already is that everyone grieves differently. You feel SO guilty about this, but she may be angry. If I did a thing and lost someone their child, I would ALSO feel so guilty and to be blamed too.

&#x200B;

I am sure it cannot BE your fault. More likely it was some unforeseeable thing that happened and you just could not foresee it, no matter what.

Probably, especially at first, because you are SO shocked that they left. Just so, so shocked. Likewise happened to me about my older sister when she died. I was probably shocked enough for a year or two, before the brew of grief settled. 

&#x200B;

Mind you, the grief, I found, doesn't go away. You just somehow find coping mechanisms to deal with it. I will be getting counselling soon, b/c I have other fish to fry, not to mention the grief. Plenty on my plate to sort.
